{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1263222-perfecting-living-matter","id":1263222,"title":"Perfecting Living matter","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-28T11:46:20-07:00","id":1263222,"title":"Perfecting Living matter","content":"A doctor, who's also a Moros, extracts and perfects bone marrow from a leukaemia patient, then destroys the patient's remaining marrow and injects the patient with the perfected marrow, letting it regenerate. This is based on the normal methods of treating leukaemia. What might happen to the patient?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T13:31:22-07:00","id":1263240,"title":"","content":"Whatever the ST needs. Depending on how it\u2019s Perfected and who the patient is things could turn out fine or yuh could end up with Abyssal bone cancer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T17:16:26-07:00","id":1263284,"title":"","content":"I fail to see how the Abyss would enter into the equation unless a spell to perfect the marrow is cast in front of Sleepers who are told it is a spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T20:10:19-07:00","id":1263301,"title":"","content":"Whatever your Legacy wants to happen to them.<br /> Bone Marrow is so esoteric a bodily &quot;organ&quot; that you'd certainly need a specialized Legacy focusing on it to make that work.<br /> <br /> And unless you just want to do some kind of &quot;Bone Marrow&quot; Legacy, that could actually be a really cool/creep Lich Legacy.<br /> <br /> Extracting their organs one by one, Perfecting them with an Attainment, then surgically or magically reattaching them.<br /> Given the open dev material for Signs of Sorcery states &quot;the material does not die unless reverted to its mundane form&quot;, that could very possibly work.<br /> <br /> Possibly adding in a Reaper angle by figuring out where the seat of the soul is, if indeed there is one. Possibly to keep themselves &quot;alive&quot; while they perfect the brain, heart, and other important organs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T22:55:50-07:00","id":1263316,"title":"","content":"After extracting it, you perfect it with what and how?<br /> Life could potentially fix the cancerous cells but I don't think making that Lasting fits. <br /> Life <i>or</i> Death should be able to isolate the cancerous cells from the set, however, and isolate and kill them.<br /> Having done <i>that,</i> the remnant could be expanded with Life and reinserted. Or, for that matter, simply reinserted.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd allow a Perfecting effect guide healing such that it actually restores full function. In this case, it would need to be maintained for a few <i>months </i>to help the marrow restore selective immunity.<br /> <br /> A Death/Life conjunction could simply target the infected cells or even end the cancer <i>in</i> the cells..","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T02:03:17-07:00","id":1263322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thenate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1263222-perfecting-living-matter?p=1263316#post1263316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Death/Life conjunction could simply target the infected cells or even end the cancer <i>in</i> the cells..</div> </div> </div> </div>Just Life is all that would be required.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T02:06:30-07:00","id":1263323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1263222-perfecting-living-matter?p=1263284#post1263284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I fail to see how the Abyss would enter into the equation unless a spell to perfect the marrow is cast in front of Sleepers who are told it is a spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a Disciple who decides to rush things instead of spending their Reach wisely, and who releases the Paradox. Or maybe a Scelrsti forces the Paradox on him, etc. There are options, context matters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T02:40:09-07:00","id":1263324,"title":"","content":"The Preview would seem to indicate that it wouldn't work, though not really what would happen.<br /> <br /> I mean, looking at it, it's a little odd that the author doesn't seem to offer more consideration of blood, seeing as blood donation is pretty common. The general suggestion that living materials become symbolically dead might cover that, though that seems a little arbitrary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T03:23:54-07:00","id":1263326,"title":"","content":"Bone marrow for all needed purposes is acutally alive. What you need to cure leukaemina are the living cells of the marrow. I do not recall anything in the book about perfecting living matter. So it falls under the purview of Live and the results may varry heavily depending on how the perfecting was done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11939-hardcorehannes","name":"HardcoreHannes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"200"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T04:21:35-07:00","id":1263331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HardcoreHannes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1263222-perfecting-living-matter?p=1263326#post1263326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not recall anything in the book about perfecting living matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's from the Signs of Sorcery preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T15:45:38-07:00","id":1263431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1263222-perfecting-living-matter?p=1263322#post1263322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just Life is all that would be required.</div> </div> </div> </div>Arguably.<br /> <br /> That entirely depends on how symbolically you look at cancer.<br /> <br /> From a strictly scientific standpoint, you just need to remove the mutation/infection/misconfiguration from each cell. (Whichever type it is) One could argue that Life might be able to simply heal the damage in cells or order them to shift their control state or otherwise just fix things.<br /> <br /> I counter by pointing out the inability of Life to simply restore things that can't recover on their own. Regeneration is a fairly analogous spell effect.<br /> <br /> I'd further argue that cancer qualifies as a Death pattern intruding into a Life pattern and is, thus, resistant to the basic healing effects of just Life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Grump, grouse, and/or gripe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate","name":"thenate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar672_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T16:12:58-07:00","id":1263432,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/672-thenate\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar672_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"672\" data-vbnamecard=\"672\">thenate</a> And you\u2019d be wrong.<br /> <br /> Heck, you could kill cancer via Body Control and a bit of creativity, restrict blood and nutrients to the cancer cells so they starve for instance, or instruct your immune system to attack the cancer cells.<br /> <br /> Requiring Life and Death for something that can fall purely under the purview of one and maybe under the purview of the other (Ending the cancer via just Death for instance), is just holding onto the old conjunction paradigm of arcana in 1e, which itself is a relic from Ascension. It\u2019s an outmoded and irrelevant way of thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 10-29-2018, 07:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}